WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.720
After the Yongle Emperor, Zhu Di, took the throne, he placed great importance on the city of Beijing in the north.

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:10.480
He stood on the city wall gazing into the distance, thinking about Beijing's future.

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:15.800
The Yongle Emperor strengthened Beijing's political status and sent a large army to guard the northern frontier.

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:20.320
The soldiers were full of spirit, guarding the northern border day and night.

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:24.960
In the year 1421, the Ming dynasty officially announced the move of the capital to Beijing.

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:29.480
Bells and drums sounded together in the great hall, as civil and military officials stood neatly on both sides.

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:35.400
The grand procession moving the capital carried treasures and documents into the city of Beijing.

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:43.840
Horse-drawn carriages followed one after another, the procession stretching from the city gate into the distance.

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:48.280
From then on, Beijing long remained the shared political center of the Ming and Qing dynasties.

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:52.840
The markets were bustling with people coming and going, and the shops were filled with all kinds of goods.

00:00:52.840 --> 00:00:57.920
Beijing's city layout has had a far-reaching influence and remains very important even today.
